.TH "REPROCTL\-EXIT\-CODES" "1" "2026" "reproctl" "Repro Development Tools"
.SH NAME
reproctl\-exit\-codes \- exit code conventions for reproctl commands
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]reproctl help exit\-codes\f[R]
.SH DESCRIPTION
reproctl uses a small, fixed set of exit codes so that scripts and
agents can reliably determine the outcome of any command.
.SH EXIT CODES
.TP
\f[B]0\f[R] \(em Success
The operation completed as expected.
.TP
\f[B]1\f[R] \(em Error
The operation failed due to bad input, a runtime failure, or a missing
prerequisite.
.TP
\f[B]2\f[R] \(em User cancelled
The user cancelled an interactive prompt (Ctrl\-C in a picker, empty
input, or answering \(dqn\(dq to a confirmation that aborts the
operation).
.SH CONVENTIONS
.SS Status commands
\f[B]status\f[R], \f[B]cluster status\f[R], \f[B]db status\f[R], and
\f[B]context\f[R] are \f[I]queries\f[R] \(em they report the current
state of the system.
They return \f[B]0\f[R] when they successfully produce output, even if
the thing being checked is unhealthy or not running.
The health information is conveyed in the output, not the exit code.
.SS Health\-assertion commands
\f[B]checkhealth\f[R] and \f[B]doctor\f[R] are \f[I]assertions\f[R] \(em
they verify that the environment meets expectations.
They return \f[B]0\f[R] when all checks pass (or only warnings are
found) and \f[B]1\f[R] when errors are detected.
.SS Action commands
\f[B]start\f[R], \f[B]stop\f[R], \f[B]restart\f[R], \f[B]cluster
up\f[R], \f[B]cluster down\f[R], \f[B]cluster reset\f[R], \f[B]db
reset\f[R], \f[B]db migrate\f[R], \f[B]db seed\f[R], \f[B]wt
create\f[R], \f[B]wt remove\f[R], and \f[B]wt prune\f[R] perform a
mutation.
They return \f[B]0\f[R] on success and \f[B]1\f[R] on failure.
.SS die()
The internal \f[B]die()\f[R] helper always exits \f[B]1\f[R].
Commands that call die on fatal errors conform to the exit code table
automatically.
.SS Interactive pickers
When a command invokes an interactive picker (\f[B]\-\-pick\f[R] flag or
automatic picker on a terminal), user cancellation (Ctrl\-C in fzf,
empty input in the numbered prompt) exits \f[B]2\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
.IP
.EX
reproctl status
echo $?    # 0 \(em even if Tilt is not running

reproctl checkhealth
echo $?    # 1 if errors found, 0 otherwise

reproctl start api\-server
echo $?    # 0 on success, 1 on failure

reproctl start \-\-pick   # user presses Ctrl\-C
echo $?    # 2

reproctl db status
echo $?    # 0 \(em even if Tilt is not running
.EE
